course: dictionary
lesson: 15178
title: Sculling: rowing and floating
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words belong to a sport, or to one special activity. Sculling is one of them. Its meaning depends on the place you find it, so the words around it are the clues. «The rowers spent the morning sculling along the river.» Rowers sit in a boat and pull oars, so here sculling means rowing a boat.
explain: In a swimming pool, sculling means something different. «Tom stayed afloat in the deep end by sculling with his hands.» Tom is not rowing anything. He is moving his hands back and forth in the water to keep himself up, so sculling is a way of floating.
explain: Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence. Does «Tom stayed afloat by moving his hands back and forth» still make sense? Yes, so you have found the right meaning. Always ask what the sentence is about: a boat, or the water.
fact: Sculling means rowing a boat with two oars, one in each hand, or with a single oar at the back of the boat.
fact: A sculling boat is a long, thin boat built for rowing fast.
fact: In swimming lessons, sculling means moving your hands back and forth in the water to float or tread water.
fact: Single sculls is a rowing race for one rower in one boat.
fact: «Sculling» is a noun for the activity and a verb, «scull», for the action: «She sculls every morning.»
exercise: «The rowers spent the morning sculling along the river.» What does sculling mean here? | Riding a bike fast | *Rowing a boat with oars | Singing loudly | Painting a fence
exercise: In swimming class, Mia learns sculling to stay up in the deep end. What does sculling mean in swimming? | Kicking as fast as she can | Holding her breath under the water | *Moving her hands back and forth in the water | Diving to the bottom of the pool
exercise: «Ana won the single sculls race.» Which word tells you the boat has only one rower? | *single | race | won | Ana
test: «Tom stayed afloat in the deep end by sculling with his hands.» What does sculling mean in this sentence? | Jumping off the diving board | Sinking slowly to the bottom | *Moving his hands back and forth in the water to stay up | Shouting for help
test: «The sculling boat glided over the lake.» What is a sculling boat? | A boat with a sail | *A long, thin boat built for rowing | A big ferry with a engine | A rubber dinghy for children
exam: «Lily's club trains for sculling, so she can row a single sculls boat in the summer race.» What does sculling mean in this sentence? | *Rowing a boat with oars | Painting the club's boats | Swimming on her back in the pool | Jumping into the lake
